round it, and a big double-eaved dark tiled roof with sweeping upturned corners and ridge ornaments, reaching 20m. A long vermilion banner with a gold flame emblem hangs flat over the FRONT face of the right pylon. Two simple guardian reliefs set flat into the pylons beside the passage. A short flight of stone steps at the foot of the passage. PROPORTIONS: FRONT and BACK views about 0.7 times as wide as tall; LEFT and RIGHT views about 0.6 times as wide as tall.",
